course: dictionary
lesson: 13543
title: Long words, clear clues
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Long words can look hard, but you can break them into parts and look for clues. Impracticable starts with im-, which often means not, and practicable is close to practical. So you can guess it is about things that cannot be done in real life.
explain: «The plan to build a bridge across the sea in one week was impracticable.» Ask yourself: what would fit here? A plan that cannot be carried out, because it is too hard, too costly or too slow. That is what impracticable means.
explain: «The road was impracticable after the flood.» Here it means the road could not be used at all. Impracticable can describe a plan, an idea or a road. In every case it means it cannot be done or used in practice, even if it sounds good on paper.
fact: Impracticable means impossible to do or carry out in practice, even if it sounds good.
fact: «Impracticable» can also describe a road or path that is impossible to use, as in «the road was impracticable after the flood».
fact: Practice here means real life: an idea can sound clever but still be impracticable.
fact: «Impracticable» is a formal word, often used in reports and history, about plans that fail because of cost, time, danger or difficulty.
fact: Useful phrases include «an impracticable plan», «prove impracticable» and «impracticable in practice».
exercise: «Building a bridge across the sea in one week was impracticable.» What does impracticable mean here? | *Impossible to carry out in real life | Painted bright blue | Very cheap and easy to build | Very beautiful to look at
exercise: The class said flying to school on a kite was impracticable. What does this suggest? | It was in the newspaper | It would be very fast | It was the best idea ever | *It could not be done in real life
exercise: Which word in «The road was impracticable after the flood» tells you the road could not be used? | flood | road | *impracticable | after
test: The plan would take fifty years, so it was impracticable. What does impracticable mean? | Very colourful | Short and quick | Easy to do | *Impossible to carry out in practice
test: Which phrase fits a plan that cannot be carried out? | a sunny day | a loud noise | *an impracticable plan | a cheap, easy idea
exam: Why would a formal report use impracticable instead of «it won't work»? | *It is a precise, formal word for a plan that cannot be carried out | It is a shorter word than any other | It is only used in stories about dragons | It means something is very cheap
